MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Crazy Life feels like a natural next choice because Home Free's vocal harmonies connect with what I enjoyed about The New Old Fashioned.",
    "Stages, Partners, and the Vince Gill collection appeal to my interest in vocal performances, even though Home Free is the strongest match for this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "20 Gospel Favourites does not match my current intent just because I previously listened to Christmas music; seasonal listening does not necessarily mean I want gospel.",
    "Wit & Wisdom Of Andy Griffith offers spoken humor when I want music, while titles like Chloe and Legends give me too little evidence of a connection to the vocal sound I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My older Christmas listening seems to have been treated as a broad interest in religious music.",
    "Broad connections to country music or vocal performers seem to count too much when the particular harmony-focused sound matters more to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with The New Old Fashioned is a stronger clue to what I want now than the Christmas albums I explored nearly two years earlier.",
    "I rarely choose something without a clear connection to my interests; Home Free's familiar vocal harmonies give me that connection, while a generally appealing singer or duet album is not enough today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in vocal music but missed how strongly my current choice favors Home Free's harmonies over older seasonal interests or broad musical similarities."
}
